{"diagnosis": "Loopback with divider 64 sent 0xa5 but recv_buf_data latched 0xe0, causing uart data mismatch trap and tohost FAIL 0xdead. States 10 and default in the excerpt compare recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4) (~4 cycles) instead of the full bit period cfg_divider (~64) used by the start-bit half-period check 2*recv_divcnt > cfg_divider, so RX advances ~16x too fast and samples the start bit. This shifts zeros with late data-bit ones into MSBs yielding 0xe0; fixing both compares to cfg_divider restores correct bit timing.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -89,14 +89,14 @@
 				10: begin
-					if (recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)) begin
+					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_buf_data <= recv_pattern;
 						recv_buf_valid <= 1;
 						recv_state <= 0;
 					end
 				end
 				default: begin
-					if (recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)) begin
+					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_pattern <= {ser_rx, recv_pattern[7:1]};
 						recv_state <= recv_state + 1;
 						recv_divcnt <= 0;
 					end
 				end
", "expected": "tohost PASS (instead of FAIL 0xdead), no uart data mismatch trap, loopback shows got 0xa5 want 0xa5"}

